        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Insert already-received fragments to fragment set.</para>
<para>Functionally equivalent to calling <ref refid="classFragmentSet_1a9c0950a289cc4e650311ed8b96350eff" kindref="member">FragmentSet::InsertFragment()</ref> (see docs for details) on each fragment covered by the report segment reception claims. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>fragmentSet</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The fragment set to modify. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>reportSegment</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The report segment. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>True if the fragment set was modified, or False otherwise. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="post"><para>If returns True, the argument to fragmentSet is modified accordingly (see above for details). </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="post"><para>Calling both <ref refid="classLtpFragmentSet_1a661a3f731e35df11c59c8e85cbd9c8bf" kindref="member">LtpFragmentSet::AddReportSegmentToFragmentSet()</ref> and <ref refid="classLtpFragmentSet_1ada2811b07ce34a1502a2233d04d19364" kindref="member">LtpFragmentSet::AddReportSegmentToFragmentSetNeedingResent()</ref> in any order on the same report segment and fragment set, will result in the fragment set containing a single fragment spanning the entire scope of the report segment. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
